1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:01,760
智驾芯片的算力，
Self-driving chips:

2
00:00:01,760 --> 00:00:03,880
有人能吹到真实的七倍。
some makers inflate compute to seven times the real number.

3
00:00:03,880 --> 00:00:05,220
这话不是我说的，
Not my words.

4
00:00:05,220 --> 00:00:08,370
是地平线创始人余凯昨晚在微博上说的。
Horizon Robotics founder Yu Kai said it on Weibo last night.

5
00:00:08,370 --> 00:00:10,690
他还给这种数字起了个名字：
He even gave that number a name:

6
00:00:10,690 --> 00:00:11,700
吹牛算力。
bragging compute.

7
00:00:11,700 --> 00:00:13,190
今天的烧脑问题：
Today's brain teaser:

8
00:00:13,190 --> 00:00:16,470
同一块芯片，算力怎么能有好几个数？
how can one chip have several compute numbers?

9
00:00:16,470 --> 00:00:17,730
先说算力是啥。
First, what is compute?

10
00:00:17,730 --> 00:00:20,910
单位叫TOPS，每秒一万亿次运算。
The unit is TOPS: a trillion operations per second.

11
00:00:20,910 --> 00:00:23,760
车上的AI看路，靠的是神经网络，
Car AI sees the road with neural networks,

12
00:00:23,760 --> 00:00:26,550
而神经网络几乎全是乘法和加法。
and those are almost all multiply and add.

13
00:00:26,550 --> 00:00:29,040
想象芯片里有一大群搬砖工人，
Picture a crowd of brick carriers inside the chip,

14
00:00:29,040 --> 00:00:30,760
每人每次搬一块砖。
each carrying one brick at a time.

15
00:00:30,760 --> 00:00:32,800
工人数乘以每秒搬几趟，
Workers times trips per second

16
00:00:32,800 --> 00:00:35,150
就是稠密算力，实打实的。
is dense compute. The honest number.

17
00:00:35,150 --> 00:00:37,330
反转一：英伟达自己就先乘了二。
Twist one: Nvidia already doubles it.

18
00:00:37,330 --> 00:00:40,940
Orin X稠密算力一百二十七，标称二百五十四。
Orin X: 127 dense, 254 on the label.

19
00:00:40,940 --> 00:00:41,900
为啥能乘二？
Why double?

20
00:00:41,900 --> 00:00:45,050
一般认为，是因为神经网络里很多数是零。
Generally, because many numbers in a neural network are zero.

21
00:00:45,050 --> 00:00:46,590
零乘什么都是零，
Zero times anything is zero,

22
00:00:46,590 --> 00:00:49,010
这块砖不用搬，直接跳过。
so that brick can be skipped.

23
00:00:49,010 --> 00:00:50,490
要是一半的数是零，
If half the numbers are zero,

24
00:00:50,490 --> 00:00:52,410
搬一半，就算搬了全部。
carrying half counts as carrying all.

25
00:00:52,410 --> 00:00:53,550
这叫稀疏算力。
That's sparse compute.

26
00:00:53,550 --> 00:00:55,960
前提是，砖真的有一半是空的。
It only works if half the bricks really are empty.

27
00:00:55,960 --> 00:00:57,880
反转二：有人乘了六七倍。
Twist two: some multiply by six or seven.

28
00:00:57,880 --> 00:00:59,920
余凯说，这就叫等效算力。
Yu calls that equivalent compute.

29
00:00:59,920 --> 00:01:02,130
比如地平线自家的征程6P，
Take Horizon's own Journey 6P:

30
00:01:02,130 --> 00:01:04,120
等效算力一千九百六十。
1960 equivalent TOPS.

31
00:01:04,120 --> 00:01:05,560
按英伟达的算法，
By Nvidia's method,

32
00:01:05,560 --> 00:01:06,950
它是五百六十。
it is 560.

33
00:01:06,950 --> 00:01:09,480
再除以二，稠密算力大约二百八十，
Halve that: about 280 dense.

34
00:01:09,480 --> 00:01:11,820
一千九百六十正好是它的七倍。
1960 is exactly seven times that.

35
00:01:11,820 --> 00:01:13,530
多出来的倍数从哪来？
Where do the extra multiples come from?

36
00:01:13,530 --> 00:01:15,530
各家没公开统一的算法。
There's no public, shared formula.

37
00:01:15,530 --> 00:01:16,780
大致的思路是：
Roughly, the idea is:

38
00:01:16,780 --> 00:01:19,560
我的工人更聪明，一个顶好几个。
my workers are smarter, one does the job of several.

39
00:01:19,560 --> 00:01:21,560
比如用更短的数字来算，
Say, computing with shorter numbers,

40
00:01:21,560 --> 00:01:24,760
或者架构更省事，就说相当于多少倍。
or a leaner design, then claiming it equals more.

41
00:01:24,760 --> 00:01:26,430
就像一台发动机说：
Like an engine saying:

42
00:01:26,430 --> 00:01:29,340
我特别省油，所以等效一千马力。
I'm so fuel efficient, call me a thousand horsepower.

43
00:01:29,340 --> 00:01:30,970
听着好像有点道理，
Sounds almost reasonable,

44
00:01:30,970 --> 00:01:33,080
可马力表上不能这么写。
but you can't print that on a spec sheet.

45
00:01:33,080 --> 00:01:34,780
反转三，最反直觉：
Twist three, the most surprising:

46
00:01:34,780 --> 00:01:37,740
就算是稠密算力，也常常用不满。
even dense compute often goes unused.

47
00:01:37,740 --> 00:01:38,610
工人再多，
However many workers you have,

48
00:01:38,610 --> 00:01:40,810
砖送不过来，也只能干等。
if bricks don't arrive, they just wait.

49
00:01:40,810 --> 00:01:42,330
这个送砖的速度，
That brick delivery speed

50
00:01:42,330 --> 00:01:43,600
叫内存带宽。
is called memory bandwidth.

51
00:01:43,600 --> 00:01:46,560
报道里说，真实效果还要看芯片利用率、
Reports note real performance also depends on utilization,

52
00:01:46,560 --> 00:01:47,830
编译器和软件。
compilers and software.

53
00:01:47,830 --> 00:01:48,880
所以，纸面算力
So, paper compute

54
00:01:48,880 --> 00:01:50,340
不等于能用的算力。
is not usable compute.

55
00:01:50,340 --> 00:01:51,920
余凯的办法很直接：
Yu's fix is simple:

56
00:01:51,920 --> 00:01:54,140
以后地平线两个数一起标。
Horizon will print both numbers.

57
00:01:54,140 --> 00:01:55,580
一个叫NV算力，
One is Nvidia-style compute:

58
00:01:55,580 --> 00:01:56,950
就是稠密乘二。
dense times two.

59
00:01:56,950 --> 00:01:58,610
另一个叫等效算力，
The other is equivalent compute,

60
00:01:58,610 --> 00:02:00,750
他自己管它叫吹牛算力。
which he himself calls bragging compute.

61
00:02:00,750 --> 00:02:03,210
友情提示：等效算力怎么折算，
Fine print: how equivalent compute is calculated,

62
00:02:03,210 --> 00:02:06,320
今天讲的是大致思路，不是官方公式。
today is the rough idea, not an official formula.

63
00:02:06,320 --> 00:02:07,520
芯片好不好，
Is a chip good?

64
00:02:07,520 --> 00:02:10,040
最后还得看车开得好不好。
In the end, ask how well the car drives.

65
00:02:10,040 --> 00:02:12,730
同一块芯片，为啥有好几个算力？
Why does one chip have several numbers?

66
00:02:12,730 --> 00:02:14,820
因为数砖的方法不一样。
Because people count bricks differently.

67
00:02:14,820 --> 00:02:16,760
下次看到几千TOPS，
Next time you see thousands of TOPS,

68
00:02:16,760 --> 00:02:20,120
先问一句：这是搬的砖，还是吹的牛？
ask: bricks carried, or bull blown?

